## Tracking progress

Progress across iterations is tracked in a **beads issue**, not in a local state
file. Never create or update a `*.md` progress/state file for this loop.
{{- if .BeadsIssue }}

This conversation is linked to beads issue `{{ .BeadsIssue }}` — that bead is the
tracking issue for this loop. Read it before doing anything else:

```bash
bd show {{ .BeadsIssue }} --long --json --include-comments
```
{{- else }}

No beads issue is linked to this conversation yet. On your **first** iteration:

1. Look for an existing bead that already covers this {{ .Noun }}
   (`bd list --status open --json`, `bd show <id>`); reuse it if you find one.
2. Otherwise create one describing the {{ .Noun }} you are about to {{ .Verb }}:

   ```bash
   bd create "<short title>" -t task -p 1 --body-file <path>
   ```

   (`bd` has **no** `@file` expansion for `-d/--description` — use
   `--body-file` or `--stdin` for anything longer than one line.)
3. Link it to this conversation so later iterations find it:
   `mitto_conversation_update(self_id: "{{ .SessionID }}", conversation_id: "self", beads_issue: "<bead id>")`.

On every later iteration, re-read that bead first
(`bd show <id> --long --json --include-comments`) instead of re-deriving state.
{{- end }}

Each iteration, record the increment on the tracking bead:

```bash
bd comment <bead id> "<what was {{ .Verb }}ed this iteration, what was verified, what remains>"
```

Use the bead's comments as the "Progress" log and its description /
acceptance criteria as the "Issues remaining" list — update the description with
`bd update <bead id> --body-file <path>` when the remaining work changes
materially. When the {{ .Noun }} is fully resolved and verified, close it with
`bd close <bead id>`.

If a requirement is genuinely ill-defined, record it as a comment on the tracking
bead, report it, and stop — never guess.
